# KSU systemless-modules overlay: the kernel loop-mounts
# /data/adb/overlayfs/overlayfs.img (labeled adb_data_file), so the loop worker
# thread does both the reads AND the writes for that image from the kernel
# domain. adb_data_file is a public type; kernel is a coredomain, so this lives
# in system_ext/private (plat-side) rather than vendor sepolicy.
#
# This was `:file read` only. That is enough to mount the image but not to write
# it back, and a refused writeback cannot be reported as "SELinux said no" by the
# loop driver -- it surfaces as a block error on perfectly healthy flash, then
# takes the image's journal down with it. Proven on sunfish, which carried the
# identical read-only rule:
#
#   avc: denied { write } for path="/data/adb/overlayfs/overlayfs.img"
#     scontext=u:r:kernel:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:adb_data_file:s0 tclass=file
#   loop: Write error at byte offset 2015371264, length 4096.
#   print_req_error: I/O error, dev loop43, sector 3936272
#   JBD2: Error -5 detected when updating journal superblock for loop43-8.
#   Aborting journal on device loop43-8.
#
# An aborted journal remounts the overlay read-only, so systemless module changes
# silently stop persisting for the rest of the boot.
allow kernel adb_data_file:file rw_file_perms;
